    concepts: ["In-order traversal","BST in-order is sorted"],
    intuition: "An in-order traversal of a BST visits values in sorted order, so walk left as far as possible, then pop nodes one at a time; the kth node popped is the kth smallest.",
    inputOutput: ["root of a BST; k, a 1-based rank.","Return the kth smallest node value.","Input: root = [3,1,4,null,2], k = 1\nOutput: 1"],
