    inputOutput: ["board: a 9×9 grid of digits \"1\"–\"9\" and \".\" for empty.","Return true if no filled digit repeats within its row, column, or box.","Input: a board where 5 appears twice in column 0\nOutput: false"],
    conceptChoices: ["A seen-set for each row, column, and box","Sort each row and check for repeats","Solve the puzzle and see if it is consistent"],
    algorithm: ["Keep nine seen-sets each for rows, columns, and 3×3 boxes.","Scan every cell; skip the empty (\".\" ) ones.","Compute the box index from the row and column.","If the digit already appears in this row, column, or box set, the board is invalid.","Otherwise record the digit in all three sets and continue."],
    fixes: ["Map (r, c) to a box index with floor(r/3)*3 + floor(c/3).","A repeat in ANY of the three units is a violation, so combine the checks with OR."],
