    concepts: ["Two pointers","Water bounded by the shorter side"],
    intuition: "Water above a bar is limited by the shorter of the tallest walls to its left and right. Walk two pointers inward and always advance the shorter side, because that side’s max is what caps the water there.",
    inputOutput: ["height: non-negative bar heights.","Return the total trapped water.","Input: height = [0,1,0,2,1,0,1,3,2,1,2,1]\nOutput: 6"],
    conceptChoices: ["Two pointers, advancing the shorter side","Sort the bars by height first","Try every left/right wall pair"],
    algorithm: ["Put one pointer at each end and track the running max height on each side.","While the pointers have not met, compare the two current heights.","If the left bar is shorter, its side is the binding wall — update leftMax.","Add leftMax minus the current height (the water above this bar), then move left inward.","Otherwise do the mirror image on the right side."],
    fixes: ["Advance the SHORTER side, since it bounds the trapped water.","Water above a bar is its side-max minus its own height."],
    complexity: "Time O(n); space O(1).",
